        "original_id": "965c6f31-7267-5190-8fcb-2f072b974567",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Richard Llewellyn, Saki, Hector Hugh Munro, Richard Dafydd Vivian Llewellyn Lloyd\n- Works: Green, Green My Valley Now\n- Roles: British novelist, British writer, pen names\n- Topics: Edwardian society and culture\n\nFacts:\n- Hector Hugh Munro was born on 18 December 1870 and died on 14 November 1916.\n- Hector Hugh Munro was better known by the pen name Saki and also frequently as H. H. Munro.\n- Saki was a British writer whose witty, mischievous, and sometimes macabre stories satirize Edwardian society and culture.\n- Richard Dafydd Vivian Llewellyn Lloyd was born on 8 December 1906 and died on 30 November 1983.\n- Richard Dafydd Vivian Llewellyn Lloyd was known by his pen name Richard Llewellyn.\n- Richard Llewellyn was a British novelist.\n- Green, Green My Valley Now is a 1975 novel by Richard Llewellyn.",
